1
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:12,833
-Thanks for your hard work.
-You're welcome.

2
00:00:12,916 --> 00:00:15,250
Bye. Why is the pretty one not here today?

3
00:00:15,916 --> 00:00:17,250
Why do you ask?

4
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:18,166
Careful now.

5
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:19,833
Her lover's right next to you.

6
00:00:21,083 --> 00:00:22,041
That way.

7
00:00:22,583 --> 00:00:23,708
Oh.

8
00:00:23,791 --> 00:00:26,583
Hey, who are you guys anyway?
How can I help you?

9
00:00:26,666 --> 00:00:29,666
-What do you know about Yuan Tao?
-It's impenetrable.

10
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:32,041
Advisers like me can't profit from it.

11
00:00:32,125 --> 00:00:35,458
Investors are getting out of stocks now
and buying up cryptocurrency.

12
00:00:35,541 --> 00:00:36,666
They caused that.

13
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:39,541
Yuan Tao set up a separate company
called Tolita. You know it?

14
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:41,375
-So they're related.
-Yep.

15
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,875
You both do the same job. You run scams.

16
00:00:46,958 --> 00:00:49,500
No wonder they could
set up shop in a prime location.

17
00:00:50,125 --> 00:00:52,666
We wanna scam Tolita,
and we need your help.

18
00:00:54,083 --> 00:00:56,666
After it's done, you'll get a big cut.

19
00:00:57,875 --> 00:01:00,250
So the plan is to scam a competitor.

20
00:01:01,208 --> 00:01:03,583
They know what they're doing. Big job.

21
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:05,916
I'll need my deposit up front.

22
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,250
Send the money to my account
within three days.

23
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:09,916
Money's no issue.

24
00:01:11,791 --> 00:01:13,958
New waves pushed the old ones ahead.

25
00:01:14,041 --> 00:01:15,416
Speaking as an old one,

26
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:17,958
it is indeed an honor
to learn from the new.

27
00:01:19,333 --> 00:01:20,166
Huh?

28
00:01:22,458 --> 00:01:23,958
Don't scam us, all right?

29
00:01:26,583 --> 00:01:28,708
There is an exciting
investment opportunity

30
00:01:28,791 --> 00:01:30,416
known as Do Bit.

31
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,875
We've all heard that, since 2009,

32
00:01:32,958 --> 00:01:35,375
Bitcoin has experienced tremendous growth.

33
00:01:35,458 --> 00:01:38,916
In 2024, it broke the $100,000…

34
00:01:57,083 --> 00:01:59,250
THE FIXERS

35
00:02:00,541 --> 00:02:03,916
DIAMOND ICE

36
00:02:06,625 --> 00:02:09,500
A little while ago,
a friend who's a seafood supplier

37
00:02:09,583 --> 00:02:12,458
sent a link to an investing influencer.

38
00:02:12,541 --> 00:02:15,291
I looked online,
and she seemed to check out.

39
00:02:16,125 --> 00:02:19,791
She teaches classes
to students focusing on cryptocurrency.

40
00:02:19,875 --> 00:02:22,666
Says she's using
the teach-men-to-fish method.

41
00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:25,375
She draws you in,
then gives you a taste of success.

42
00:02:25,458 --> 00:02:28,708
She gives you
a small amount of free cryptocurrency

43
00:02:28,791 --> 00:02:31,166
that you can invest by using their app.

44
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:34,791
Then they drive up the price,
so it looks like you're making a profit.

45
00:02:35,541 --> 00:02:36,708
-Four Circles.
-Pung.

46
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:40,666
Later, I discovered
she didn't give us any fishing rods

47
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:42,291
or even any fish.

48
00:02:42,375 --> 00:02:45,666
I was the target.
Why did I take the hook? Ugh.

49
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:48,208
-Six Circles.
-And pung.

50
00:02:48,291 --> 00:02:50,833
-Are you listening to this?
-Yeah, who says I'm not?

51
00:02:51,416 --> 00:02:54,250
Later, I discovered
the app was also a fake.

52
00:02:54,333 --> 00:02:56,166
That graph was a lie.

53
00:02:56,250 --> 00:02:58,875
And when I said I wanted to sell,
you know what she told me?

54
00:02:58,958 --> 00:03:01,791
"Oh, I'm so sorry. Our system is down."

55
00:03:01,875 --> 00:03:05,416
Then she had the nerve to say,
"Now we've frozen your account."

56
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:08,625
From what I'm hearing,
every con is identical to the other.

57
00:03:08,708 --> 00:03:09,833
Look. Nine.

58
00:03:09,916 --> 00:03:12,708
I win. Thanks for your support, buddy.

59
00:03:14,916 --> 00:03:16,666
Actually, it wasn't just me.

60
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:19,708
A lot of my seafood clients
also got caught up in it.

61
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:21,416
That's not right.

62
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:24,375
What's not right? It's no real surprise.
You're a terrible player.

63
00:03:24,458 --> 00:03:26,625
From his discards,
it's clear where he messed up.

64
00:03:27,958 --> 00:03:29,958
You discard a tile
and gave him the winning one.

65
00:03:30,041 --> 00:03:31,000
-Why?
-Yeah, why?

66
00:03:31,083 --> 00:03:35,791
What I meant was, if the app's fake,
it's not impossible no one saw.

67
00:03:35,875 --> 00:03:38,041
I was listening, all right.

68
00:03:38,125 --> 00:03:40,333
You're very good at memorizing tiles,
aren't you?

69
00:03:40,416 --> 00:03:43,083
In the moment,
everyone just wants to make money,

70
00:03:43,166 --> 00:03:44,416
and then it turns out

71
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:45,875
the whole thing's a lie.

72
00:03:45,958 --> 00:03:47,541
It's not like you're any different.

73
00:03:47,625 --> 00:03:52,125
You happily discarded the wrong tile,
and then… he wiped you out.

74
00:03:53,583 --> 00:03:54,416
Hey.

75
00:03:56,291 --> 00:03:57,958
Why are you asking about this?

76
00:03:58,041 --> 00:04:00,333
Just because.

77
00:04:00,416 --> 00:04:03,000
We're running a campaign
for staff about fraud.

78
00:04:03,083 --> 00:04:04,875
Oh, good for you!

79
00:04:05,791 --> 00:04:06,958
You should take it.

80
00:04:07,041 --> 00:04:10,250
Hey, now don't make me look bad
in front of your boss.

81
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:13,083
Don't be embarrassed. You really need it.

82
00:04:15,708 --> 00:04:17,791
Why do you need to see me so suddenly?

83
00:04:17,875 --> 00:04:19,875
Uh, I wanted to check how you were going

84
00:04:19,958 --> 00:04:21,750
with the search for Gerald.

85
00:04:21,833 --> 00:04:25,041
That's what this is about.
I thought I was in trouble.

86
00:04:25,125 --> 00:04:27,041
Oh, well, we found out

87
00:04:27,125 --> 00:04:30,625
the founder of Yuan Tao, Zoe,
was linked to Gerald.

88
00:04:30,708 --> 00:04:33,708
And the time of Zoe's death coincides
with the disappearance of Gerald.

89
00:04:34,708 --> 00:04:35,750
We also found out

90
00:04:35,833 --> 00:04:38,875
that Zoe and her partner William
had a falling out.

91
00:04:38,958 --> 00:04:41,041
We're working on a way
of getting close to William.

92
00:04:41,125 --> 00:04:43,166
I assume you have a plan.

93
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:46,458
William has set up another company
called Tolita that runs scams.

94
00:04:46,541 --> 00:04:49,750
We wanna use Tolita
to find proof of his fraud.

95
00:04:49,833 --> 00:04:52,291
Then we can force him
to tell us more about Zoe.

96
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:53,208
Ah.

97
00:04:54,791 --> 00:04:56,958
Uh, I heard from Fixer Gold

98
00:04:57,041 --> 00:05:00,458
that Gerald is connected
to the survival of Ching He.

99
00:05:00,541 --> 00:05:02,625
Uh, is that right?

100
00:05:05,375 --> 00:05:08,250
There are two types of people
in this world who are the most dangerous.

101
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:09,333
Yeah.

102
00:05:09,416 --> 00:05:12,541
First type possess crucial information.

103
00:05:12,625 --> 00:05:16,541
The second type
are those who know what they shouldn't.

104
00:05:17,875 --> 00:05:21,500
Oh, then pretend I never raised it.

105
00:05:21,583 --> 00:05:24,458
I wanna live a little longer.

106
00:05:24,541 --> 00:05:26,208
I'll go now.

107
00:05:27,291 --> 00:05:29,041
Pretend I never asked.

108
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:38,666
ZOE

109
00:05:42,541 --> 00:05:44,041
Oh. Hey, Ben.

110
00:05:44,541 --> 00:05:46,666
Did you open the arcade
or the stall first?

111
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:50,000
-This stall was left to me by my father.
-Mm.

112
00:05:50,083 --> 00:05:53,500
-He passed, and then I took it over.
-Oh.

113
00:05:53,583 --> 00:05:56,625
The arcade I took on after I retired.

114
00:05:56,708 --> 00:05:58,375
What did you do before?

115
00:05:59,583 --> 00:06:00,833
Mina hasn't said anything?

116
00:06:01,458 --> 00:06:02,583
I was once a fixer.

117
00:06:04,875 --> 00:06:07,250
-You were a fixer? She didn't say.
-Mm-hmm.

118
00:06:07,333 --> 00:06:11,041
We haven't said more than ten words
to each other. You think she's difficult?

119
00:06:11,125 --> 00:06:14,958
Don't you think bad-mouthing people
behind their backs is improper?

120
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:17,208
The usual?

121
00:06:18,333 --> 00:06:19,291
Hmm.

122
00:06:22,708 --> 00:06:23,541
What's the usual?

123
00:06:24,166 --> 00:06:27,875
Tien-bu-la. No pork meatballs or radish.

124
00:06:27,958 --> 00:06:30,208
If you don't want pork or radish,
why have tien-bu-la?

125
00:06:30,291 --> 00:06:32,208
If she doesn't want it, I'll have it.

126
00:06:33,833 --> 00:06:35,708
There you are. Want some?

127
00:06:35,791 --> 00:06:36,666
Oh, sure.

128
00:06:37,708 --> 00:06:39,541
-What would you like?
-Tien-bu-la.

129
00:06:40,125 --> 00:06:42,250
No blood pudding. No deep-fried tofu.

130
00:06:43,375 --> 00:06:45,416
No blood pudding. No deep-fried tofu.

131
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:46,625
For crying out loud.

132
00:06:46,708 --> 00:06:49,000
Are difficult people always picky eaters?

133
00:06:50,250 --> 00:06:53,208
Young these days.
They don't eat this. They don't eat that.

134
00:06:53,291 --> 00:06:54,583
-It's a pain in the ass.
-Hey.

135
00:06:54,666 --> 00:06:56,458
Don't use two bowls. Just combine them.

136
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:58,833
-Combine.
-Yeah, just do what I say.

137
00:06:58,916 --> 00:07:01,333
Here. There was just one bowl left.

138
00:07:01,916 --> 00:07:03,708
You two can make do. Eat together.

139
00:07:04,416 --> 00:07:05,583
Eat together.

140
00:07:11,750 --> 00:07:14,250
This app already shows a 15% profit.

141
00:07:14,333 --> 00:07:16,458
You're a fast mover.
You've already invested.

142
00:07:16,541 --> 00:07:17,583
I bought it.

143
00:07:18,416 --> 00:07:20,625
I got Ben to contact the crypto dealers

144
00:07:20,708 --> 00:07:22,166
and convert the money into Bitcoin.

145
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:26,041
And I've downloaded the app. Look here.

146
00:07:26,125 --> 00:07:30,333
Ben's graph is trending lower
than mine is, having not bought in.

147
00:07:30,833 --> 00:07:31,958
That's not right.

148
00:07:32,041 --> 00:07:33,541
If they wanna scam people,

149
00:07:33,625 --> 00:07:36,791
then buyers should see
a significant price increase.

150
00:07:37,583 --> 00:07:39,000
Gradual increases are the way.

151
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:42,375
Quick increases encourage people
to cash out their profits.

152
00:07:42,458 --> 00:07:46,083
This con relies on the knowledge
that mostly earning less hurts more.

153
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:47,541
It's the law of greed.

154
00:07:47,625 --> 00:07:49,375
Looks like a stroll to heaven.

155
00:07:49,458 --> 00:07:51,375
Turns out to be
a one-way ticket to prison.

156
00:07:51,458 --> 00:07:54,583
Hey. This just proves
that Tolita runs scams.

157
00:07:54,666 --> 00:07:57,041
But it still doesn't connect back
to William.

158
00:07:57,125 --> 00:08:00,041
This Dolly's
not just a spokesperson or a figurehead.

159
00:08:00,125 --> 00:08:02,541
She's essentially running the whole thing.

160
00:08:03,208 --> 00:08:05,083
-We need to lure William out.
-Uh…

161
00:08:06,125 --> 00:08:08,166
Then we need an even bigger mark.

162
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:09,666
Yeah.

163
00:08:14,458 --> 00:08:17,125
Don't look at me.
I'm already five million in debt.

164
00:08:25,083 --> 00:08:26,083
Thirty million.

165
00:08:26,166 --> 00:08:27,416
Oh fuck.

166
00:08:27,916 --> 00:08:30,291
HUNG KUO-LUNG'S INVESTMENT PHILOSOPHY
RESUME

167
00:08:32,416 --> 00:08:35,166
Next, we need to get Hung Kuo-lung

168
00:08:35,250 --> 00:08:37,958
to get Dolly to believe
that you're an easy mark.

169
00:08:38,041 --> 00:08:40,125
I have to ask, Mr. Hung.

170
00:08:40,208 --> 00:08:42,291
Why are you working for commission
as a broker

171
00:08:42,375 --> 00:08:44,458
when you're an investment adviser?

172
00:08:44,541 --> 00:08:46,958
It's a sad story.

173
00:08:49,291 --> 00:08:52,333
My mother passed away.
It's been two weeks.

174
00:08:52,833 --> 00:08:54,000
I… I really…

175
00:08:54,083 --> 00:08:57,583
Uh, I really can't continue
managing my members' accounts,

176
00:08:57,666 --> 00:08:59,916
but I don't want to let them down either.

177
00:09:01,250 --> 00:09:02,708
What will be your commission?

178
00:09:02,791 --> 00:09:04,208
15%.

179
00:09:07,250 --> 00:09:09,541
I've never had a request like this one.

180
00:09:09,625 --> 00:09:11,375
I'm gonna have to think about it.

181
00:09:11,458 --> 00:09:12,291
10%?

182
00:09:12,958 --> 00:09:16,250
It's not the percentage,
but thanks for the suggestion.

183
00:09:18,666 --> 00:09:22,708
DUBAI, UNITED ARAB EMIRATES

184
00:09:24,750 --> 00:09:27,208
I got the feeling
she noticed something was off.

185
00:09:27,291 --> 00:09:30,500
She knew I was lying to her.
I could see it in her eyes.

186
00:09:30,583 --> 00:09:32,958
That's what we want.
To think you're lying.

187
00:09:33,041 --> 00:09:34,166
Huh?

188
00:09:34,250 --> 00:09:36,833
We want her to find out
that you're an investment fraudster.

189
00:09:36,916 --> 00:09:40,166
Because a goose that's already plucked
makes an easy meal.

190
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:43,333
The work's been done.
How could she resist making a move?

191
00:09:43,875 --> 00:09:48,750
Oh. You three hustlers hired a hustler
to hustle a bigger hustler.

192
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:51,125
Impressive, and you're the goose.

193
00:09:51,208 --> 00:09:52,500
Oh, here. Get rich.

194
00:09:53,250 --> 00:09:54,833
-Hey.
-I win.

195
00:09:55,583 --> 00:09:58,583
South Wind, Four Seasons,
and single tile weight.

196
00:09:59,083 --> 00:09:59,958
I fleeced you.

197
00:10:00,041 --> 00:10:01,416
Still think you can win?

198
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:02,625
Eat me.

199
00:10:09,583 --> 00:10:10,416
Yeah.

200
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:13,041
Hello. Is this Mr. Chiang Ming-shun?

201
00:10:13,125 --> 00:10:14,416
Sorry, wrong number.

202
00:10:15,125 --> 00:10:17,250
Hey. Hey, hey, hey, hey.

203
00:10:17,333 --> 00:10:18,833
Am I speaking with Mr. Chiang?

204
00:10:18,916 --> 00:10:22,083
Ah, I'm so sorry.
Uh, the reception was terrible just now.

205
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:25,625
Hi, I'm Dolly. I'm the CEO of Tolita.

206
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:26,958
Oh, yes, I heard.

207
00:10:27,041 --> 00:10:31,333
Uh, my investment manager, Hung Kuo-lung,
wants me to invest in your Do Bit.

208
00:10:31,416 --> 00:10:34,125
Uh, but why are you
contacting me directly?

209
00:10:34,625 --> 00:10:37,875
Because, sir, you're in
the highest investment tier with us.

210
00:10:37,958 --> 00:10:41,208
This is an invitation
for you to join us at a private dinner.

211
00:10:41,291 --> 00:10:42,708
Oh, there's no need for that.

212
00:10:42,791 --> 00:10:44,375
I'm very interested in your product,

213
00:10:44,458 --> 00:10:47,125
and I don't want to waste your time
with socializing.

214
00:10:47,208 --> 00:10:49,541
How about, uh, if you need anything,

215
00:10:49,625 --> 00:10:52,666
have your boss contact me directly
or come find me.

216
00:10:52,750 --> 00:10:54,875
Oh, sorry. I have to board a plane.

217
00:10:54,958 --> 00:10:55,833
Let's talk later.

218
00:10:55,916 --> 00:10:58,541
Mr. Chiang, let me explain. You there?

219
00:11:02,958 --> 00:11:04,375
Are you catching a plane?

220
00:11:04,958 --> 00:11:06,916
Me, no. Uh…

221
00:11:07,666 --> 00:11:11,083
-Did you see a doctor?
-My stomach's been bad.

222
00:11:11,166 --> 00:11:12,250
I've got the runs.

223
00:11:12,333 --> 00:11:15,125
You hate taking drugs.
You won't even see a doctor.

224
00:11:15,208 --> 00:11:16,041
What drugs are they?

225
00:11:16,125 --> 00:11:18,916
It's so annoying, but the doctor said
I have to take this medication.

226
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,333
If you won't say…

227
00:11:20,416 --> 00:11:21,500
-Mom!
-Oh.

228
00:11:21,583 --> 00:11:23,041
-Mom, Dad--
-Sh!

229
00:11:29,708 --> 00:11:30,708
All right.

230
00:11:31,833 --> 00:11:32,875
I'm going to tell you,

231
00:11:33,791 --> 00:11:35,208
but you must never tell your mother.

232
00:11:35,291 --> 00:11:36,208
Okay.

233
00:11:36,708 --> 00:11:37,708
Ah…

234
00:11:43,250 --> 00:11:44,208
You saw it.

235
00:11:46,375 --> 00:11:47,416
Truth is…

236
00:11:49,416 --> 00:11:51,333
-I keep shaking.
-Uh-huh.

237
00:11:51,416 --> 00:11:52,250
Look.

238
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:54,791
Why is this happening?

239
00:11:54,875 --> 00:11:55,833
Here, not here.

240
00:11:55,916 --> 00:11:57,625
I know. I'm looking over here.

241
00:11:58,666 --> 00:12:00,750
Have you heard of Parkinson's disease?

242
00:12:04,708 --> 00:12:05,708
Mm.

243
00:12:14,208 --> 00:12:15,250
Hmm.

244
00:12:32,750 --> 00:12:33,833
Sir Hong,

245
00:12:34,583 --> 00:12:38,166
every day, so many
come to pray to the deities.

246
00:12:38,250 --> 00:12:41,666
Just how many people
will receive his help?

247
00:12:42,458 --> 00:12:44,750
Heaven helps those who help themselves.

248
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:45,666
People who come here

249
00:12:46,583 --> 00:12:48,541
believe that holding a stick of incense

250
00:12:48,625 --> 00:12:52,333
and chanting a few words
will solve everything.

251
00:12:53,291 --> 00:12:54,166
Hmm.

252
00:12:54,666 --> 00:12:56,750
You've been here for many years,

253
00:12:57,250 --> 00:12:59,000
but you're not a believer.

254
00:12:59,083 --> 00:13:00,583
That's very interesting.

255
00:13:02,041 --> 00:13:05,833
I just don't believe that God
or the Buddha would help people like that.

256
00:13:06,416 --> 00:13:08,208
Those who take heaven's grace

257
00:13:08,708 --> 00:13:10,750
should have exhausted all effort.

258
00:13:14,916 --> 00:13:18,291
So in your opinion,
apart from Fixer Terra,

259
00:13:18,375 --> 00:13:20,416
who else will stand with us?

260
00:13:20,916 --> 00:13:23,291
Whose side they stand on doesn't matter.

261
00:13:23,791 --> 00:13:24,625
But

262
00:13:25,291 --> 00:13:29,833
if Tristan Hsueh is successful,
then we have an issue.

263
00:13:31,208 --> 00:13:33,708
The Hsuehs are
a prominent political family.

264
00:13:33,791 --> 00:13:36,333
They've made powerful relationships,

265
00:13:36,416 --> 00:13:39,041
have financial resources as well.

266
00:13:39,125 --> 00:13:42,541
Also, they have strong connections
with the police.

267
00:13:42,625 --> 00:13:46,166
Once Yeh Yueh Tong and the Hsueh clan
join forces and grow stronger,

268
00:13:47,125 --> 00:13:49,333
you will have to accept heaven's will.

269
00:13:51,708 --> 00:13:55,541
Even so,
I think I still have the Hsuehs in check.

270
00:13:56,333 --> 00:13:59,875
A single pawn
can't decide the chess match.

271
00:14:00,708 --> 00:14:04,416
And whether this pawn is white

272
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:06,833
or black is uncertain.

273
00:14:06,916 --> 00:14:08,666
At first, there was just one,

274
00:14:09,333 --> 00:14:12,583
but God sent another.

275
00:14:14,375 --> 00:14:16,333
You sent them to find Gerald.

276
00:14:16,416 --> 00:14:17,916
Is this the right move?

277
00:14:18,416 --> 00:14:20,000
I've done all I can,

278
00:14:20,625 --> 00:14:23,041
and now it's heaven's will.

279
00:14:36,791 --> 00:14:37,750
Hey, buddy.

280
00:14:37,833 --> 00:14:40,833
Do you really think
what I said to Dolly wasn't too harsh?

281
00:14:40,916 --> 00:14:43,000
If I've upset her,
the danger is she won't call back.

282
00:14:44,083 --> 00:14:47,000
You're in a stronger position
if you play hard to get.

283
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:50,166
Over the years,
I've learned that if you let them go,

284
00:14:50,250 --> 00:14:51,666
they actually run away.

285
00:14:51,750 --> 00:14:54,458
Hey, are you playing hard to get
with Mina?

286
00:14:54,541 --> 00:14:56,833
I'm telling you,
don't drag it out for too long.

287
00:14:56,916 --> 00:14:58,500
-In the early days--
-You must be dressed.

288
00:14:58,583 --> 00:15:01,125
-I'm done.
-Why aren't you out here?

289
00:15:03,583 --> 00:15:05,500
You like?

290
00:15:05,583 --> 00:15:06,500
A goose with flair.

291
00:15:06,583 --> 00:15:10,166
Like an old man at a wedding banquet.
Come on. Why are you wearing this tie?

292
00:15:10,250 --> 00:15:12,666
It looks good. It was the first gift
my wife ever gave me.

293
00:15:12,750 --> 00:15:13,958
And your hairstyle.

294
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,333
Why does it look like it's 50 years old?

295
00:15:16,416 --> 00:15:18,666
Because I've been doing it
for nearly 50 years.

296
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:21,000
And your gut. You need to sort that out.

297
00:15:21,083 --> 00:15:23,791
-Change into something else.
-Come on, buddy.

298
00:15:23,875 --> 00:15:26,083
This is the tenth one I've tried.

299
00:15:26,583 --> 00:15:30,083
Never mind. I'm gonna take you somewhere.
I'm sure you're going to enjoy it.

300
00:15:34,125 --> 00:15:35,416
Ya!

301
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:37,750
Hi. Hsien not here? Is he off today?

302
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:39,041
-Felix!
-Huh?

303
00:15:39,125 --> 00:15:41,333
-I can't believe you're here.
-Yeah.

304
00:15:42,083 --> 00:15:44,375
My father's been dead for three years.

305
00:15:44,458 --> 00:15:45,916
-Is that so?
-Yeah.

306
00:15:47,416 --> 00:15:49,250
Oh, I like your son's suit.

307
00:15:49,791 --> 00:15:51,583
-My son? That's a stretch.
-Yeah.

308
00:15:51,666 --> 00:15:54,041
-My son's in junior high.
-Ah.

309
00:15:54,125 --> 00:15:56,583
So, Hsien… How did it happen?

310
00:15:57,083 --> 00:16:00,666
Uh, he had a stroke,
then passed away two or three years later.

311
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:02,125
-Is that so?
-Uh-huh.

312
00:16:02,208 --> 00:16:04,083
-I guess it's been ten years.
-Mm.

313
00:16:04,166 --> 00:16:06,791
I am a colleague of his.
I'm here to help pick a suit.

314
00:16:06,875 --> 00:16:08,208
Oh, okay.

315
00:16:08,291 --> 00:16:09,750
-Let's do it.
-All right.

316
00:16:10,750 --> 00:16:12,416
Who are you working for now?

317
00:16:12,958 --> 00:16:15,083
Uh, I'm freelancing, I suppose.

318
00:16:15,166 --> 00:16:16,333
-Oh.
-Uh-huh.

319
00:16:17,333 --> 00:16:20,166
182, 94, 86, 94.

320
00:16:20,666 --> 00:16:22,791
-Oh.
-He's been touching me.

321
00:16:23,375 --> 00:16:24,916
Eight times already.

322
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,458
-Time flies.
-Sure does.

323
00:16:26,541 --> 00:16:28,000
I remember when we were younger?

324
00:16:28,083 --> 00:16:30,833
You and she would bring alcohol as a gift.

325
00:16:30,916 --> 00:16:32,541
I wanted a drink, but you wouldn't let me.

326
00:16:32,625 --> 00:16:34,416
Here. Try this one on.

327
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:37,500
Who told you
not to let Chi chase you back then?

328
00:16:37,583 --> 00:16:39,541
Ten years have gone
in the blink of an eye.

329
00:16:39,625 --> 00:16:41,791
Your dad's gone. Chi's gone too.

330
00:16:48,166 --> 00:16:49,041
That rack?

331
00:16:49,125 --> 00:16:51,750
They were custom-made for mobsters
back in the day.

332
00:16:51,833 --> 00:16:53,541
That's why it's all the same design.

333
00:16:54,416 --> 00:16:56,375
This one's very Felix Chiang.

334
00:16:56,458 --> 00:16:58,916
Oh, he used to hate wearing this style.

335
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,500
He used to have them specially made
by my dad.

336
00:17:01,583 --> 00:17:03,833
It's the thing to have custom-made.

337
00:17:03,916 --> 00:17:08,000
He keeps saying he used to be a gangster,
was a crack shooter, and was feared.

338
00:17:08,083 --> 00:17:09,125
That right?

339
00:17:09,208 --> 00:17:12,791
Felix and Chi were known
as the Black and White Impermanence.

340
00:17:13,375 --> 00:17:14,833
Cold Blood was a crack shot.

341
00:17:14,916 --> 00:17:16,000
Chi was the fighter.

342
00:17:16,083 --> 00:17:17,125
Cold Blood?

343
00:17:17,208 --> 00:17:18,250
Yeah, he chose that.

344
00:17:18,333 --> 00:17:20,666
How did he turn into such a smooth talker?

345
00:17:20,750 --> 00:17:23,833
To survive in that world,
you had to be like that.

346
00:17:23,916 --> 00:17:24,750
Hey.

347
00:17:24,833 --> 00:17:27,833
Can you two stop bad-mouthing me
while I'm getting changed?

348
00:17:27,916 --> 00:17:31,166
Ah, if nothing had happened to Chi
back then,

349
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:34,125
maybe the two of them
would still be prowling the streets.

350
00:17:42,083 --> 00:17:44,541
Here. What do you think?

351
00:17:44,625 --> 00:17:45,875
Is it all right?

352
00:17:45,958 --> 00:17:48,833
-Huh?
-Oh gosh. You look so good, Felix.

353
00:17:49,875 --> 00:17:51,208
-Finally.
-Let me see.

354
00:17:51,291 --> 00:17:52,416
How's the waistline?

355
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:53,833
No need to alter it. It's perfect.

356
00:17:53,916 --> 00:17:56,958
-What about the length?
-It's okay. I'm your average man.

357
00:17:57,041 --> 00:17:58,875
You forgot your clothes.

358
00:17:59,541 --> 00:18:01,083
I don't need them. Hmm?

359
00:18:03,041 --> 00:18:05,458
THE GENTLEMAN'S SUIT SHOP, PREMIUM SUITS

360
00:18:21,166 --> 00:18:22,250
Mr. Chiang.

361
00:18:22,750 --> 00:18:24,208
Hi. Come sit down here.

362
00:18:24,291 --> 00:18:25,291
Thank you.

363
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:26,833
Hmm.

364
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:28,958
Did you bring the manager?

365
00:18:29,041 --> 00:18:31,791
He's a crypto dealer. I run Tolita.

366
00:18:31,875 --> 00:18:34,541
You have no one above you? So you're it?

367
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:38,458
Mm-hmm. Yes, I run Tolita.

368
00:18:38,541 --> 00:18:39,375
Mm.

369
00:18:40,166 --> 00:18:41,416
And so young.

370
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:43,125
Ah. Shall we eat?

371
00:18:44,208 --> 00:18:45,041
Um…

372
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:49,125
Do you think it's unusual
that I chose this place for the meeting?

373
00:18:49,208 --> 00:18:52,125
Any place is good to discuss investments.

374
00:18:52,208 --> 00:18:53,125
Right.

375
00:18:54,125 --> 00:18:56,666
My business actually started right here.

376
00:18:56,750 --> 00:19:00,125
It was 20 years ago on this very spot.

377
00:19:00,208 --> 00:19:01,583
I had nothing.

378
00:19:02,291 --> 00:19:05,250
I could only order one plate of swamp eel
with no swamp eel.

379
00:19:07,166 --> 00:19:09,708
Then you know what I overheard
at the next table?

380
00:19:09,791 --> 00:19:12,250
They were talking about
how to venture abroad.

381
00:19:14,791 --> 00:19:18,250
Hung Kuo-lung is involved
in stock scams. Stay away from him.

382
00:19:18,750 --> 00:19:21,291
I know. That's why I asked elsewhere.

383
00:19:21,375 --> 00:19:23,125
I called Dubai and asked around.

384
00:19:23,208 --> 00:19:25,708
Reading through this, he smells fishy.

385
00:19:26,291 --> 00:19:27,500
See what he's after.

386
00:19:27,583 --> 00:19:29,708
Don't rush to commit, okay?

387
00:19:29,791 --> 00:19:31,833
Mm-hmm, got it.

388
00:19:31,916 --> 00:19:34,875
What about me?
When do I take over Yuan Tao?

389
00:19:35,750 --> 00:19:36,916
I'm sick of lying.

390
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,875
Tolita needs someone like you to run it.

391
00:19:39,958 --> 00:19:41,500
I only trust you.

392
00:19:42,541 --> 00:19:43,625
Okay?

393
00:19:43,708 --> 00:19:45,666
Mr. Chiang, I'm curious.

394
00:19:45,750 --> 00:19:48,916
In Dubai, what sort of company do you run?

395
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,166
I developed surgical technologies.

396
00:19:51,250 --> 00:19:52,208
Hmm.

397
00:19:52,708 --> 00:19:56,666
Because I did a quick check,
and I couldn't find any company output

398
00:19:56,750 --> 00:19:57,791
or cash flow.

399
00:19:59,583 --> 00:20:02,416
Ah, I should tell you.

400
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:07,166
The tech company's a front.
My real business is… games of chance.

401
00:20:08,166 --> 00:20:09,375
-Ah.
-You get me.

402
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:11,291
No wonder I couldn't find anything.

403
00:20:12,166 --> 00:20:13,791
I've always wanted to invest.

404
00:20:13,875 --> 00:20:16,083
I don't want others saying
that I'm just a gambler

405
00:20:16,166 --> 00:20:18,333
who relies on luck.

406
00:20:22,875 --> 00:20:24,000
Mr. Chiang.

407
00:20:24,083 --> 00:20:27,500
At Tolita, we do detailed searches
of every investor.

408
00:20:27,583 --> 00:20:31,375
Because, as you know, this is fairer
and safer for every investor.

409
00:20:35,750 --> 00:20:37,416
You don't believe me.

410
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,416
-I wanna be frank with you.
-Mm.

411
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:43,458
I have a few business contacts in Dubai.

412
00:20:43,541 --> 00:20:47,125
No one there
has ever heard of your business.

413
00:20:58,208 --> 00:20:59,583
Take a look, will you?

414
00:21:08,083 --> 00:21:10,416
I know how much you like cash.

415
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:12,333
Am I right?

416
00:21:12,916 --> 00:21:15,250
Hey, I trust you won't make
a mess of this.

417
00:21:15,333 --> 00:21:17,500
Mr. Chiang, you can trust us.

418
00:21:18,458 --> 00:21:20,458
All right. Dig in.

419
00:21:20,541 --> 00:21:23,083
The flavors haven't changed in 20 years.

420
00:21:23,166 --> 00:21:24,708
Come on. Don't be shy.

421
00:21:24,791 --> 00:21:28,208
I really rattled that guy,
so he had to roll out the loot.

422
00:21:28,291 --> 00:21:31,250
I tell you, that influencer was afraid
I didn't have the money.

423
00:21:31,333 --> 00:21:33,000
Once she saw the cash, she was all mine.

424
00:21:33,083 --> 00:21:36,500
She took it, we signed a contract,
and she showed me the app.

425
00:21:36,583 --> 00:21:39,333
I'm taking the cash to launder it.
I'll find you later.

426
00:21:39,416 --> 00:21:41,583
She's taking her spoils
to a money launderer now.

427
00:21:41,666 --> 00:21:42,708
Mm.

428
00:21:42,791 --> 00:21:44,041
We're following her car.

429
00:21:44,125 --> 00:21:45,208
Oh, hey.

430
00:21:45,708 --> 00:21:47,958
When you two are done tailing her,
just get here.

431
00:21:48,041 --> 00:21:49,916
I ordered too much. I can't finish it.

432
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,166
I'll even leave you two
to eat alone, okay?

433
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,875
We were once so close, and now this.

434
00:21:59,958 --> 00:22:01,541
All right, I'll eat it myself.

435
00:22:13,250 --> 00:22:14,125
For you.

436
00:22:19,916 --> 00:22:22,625
How did you know
I only eat these two things?

437
00:22:23,125 --> 00:22:26,208
I didn't.
They're just the two things I don't eat.

438
00:22:36,375 --> 00:22:37,916
The money launderer is here.

439
00:22:51,833 --> 00:22:54,333
Why not take it
to the black market and swap it for gold?

440
00:22:54,416 --> 00:22:57,833
They'll convert the money
into internationally accepted crypto,

441
00:22:57,916 --> 00:23:00,250
then put it in Dolly's overseas account.

442
00:23:00,333 --> 00:23:02,958
This way of handling,
it's more confidential.

443
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:06,750
Just because they met with that launderer
doesn't tie in William.

444
00:23:06,833 --> 00:23:08,791
How much money have you made
in your phone app?

445
00:23:08,875 --> 00:23:11,750
Around 4%. Like you said, slowly growing.

446
00:23:12,250 --> 00:23:15,208
Then I think it's time for us to shine.

447
00:23:16,583 --> 00:23:20,083
That investment last time,
I did see some profit.

448
00:23:20,166 --> 00:23:22,000
And I'm not pulling out.

449
00:23:22,083 --> 00:23:25,166
Uh, let's see if we can grow some more.

450
00:23:25,250 --> 00:23:29,083
As a businessman,
you know what long-term holding can yield,

451
00:23:29,166 --> 00:23:32,500
but you should think about
supplementing it.

452
00:23:32,583 --> 00:23:34,166
It'll increase your earnings.

453
00:23:34,250 --> 00:23:38,041
I think that as well,
but I found a target for my investing.

454
00:23:38,125 --> 00:23:41,416
This company got me 40%
in next to no time.

455
00:23:41,500 --> 00:23:42,791
He got 40.

456
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:45,000
How is that possible? You sure?

457
00:23:45,583 --> 00:23:47,375
You just can't do that well at the moment.

458
00:23:48,583 --> 00:23:51,250
Look, this is their invitation.

459
00:23:53,041 --> 00:23:54,625
It's a Singaporean company,

460
00:23:54,708 --> 00:23:56,708
but other than that,

461
00:23:56,791 --> 00:23:58,375
there's no other information.

462
00:23:58,458 --> 00:24:00,000
It's gotta be a scam.

463
00:24:01,583 --> 00:24:02,916
Go check it out.

464
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:05,958
There'll be a lot of investors.
You could take a few from them.

465
00:24:06,041 --> 00:24:06,875
Mm-hmm.

466
00:24:08,166 --> 00:24:09,750
This is your last task.

467
00:24:10,250 --> 00:24:13,083
Invite your investment clients
to a party we're having.

468
00:24:13,166 --> 00:24:14,208
That'll be easy.

469
00:24:14,291 --> 00:24:16,291
But you think William will take the bait?

470
00:24:16,375 --> 00:24:17,291
We'll find out.

471
00:24:18,208 --> 00:24:19,833
This is not all the…

472
00:24:32,166 --> 00:24:33,833
I'll definitely need your advice.

473
00:24:33,916 --> 00:24:35,625
Hey, this is the CEO.

474
00:24:35,708 --> 00:24:36,875
For someone so young,

475
00:24:36,958 --> 00:24:39,125
she has an amazing understanding
of finance.

476
00:24:39,208 --> 00:24:41,458
I'm definitely gonna need your help.

477
00:24:41,541 --> 00:24:42,958
You can just call me Mandy.

478
00:24:43,041 --> 00:24:45,958
-All right. Let's keep talking. Cheers.
-Absolutely. Okay.

479
00:24:46,041 --> 00:24:47,916
-Cheers. We'll talk later.
-Stay in touch. Okay.

480
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:49,333
-Bye now.
-Bye-bye.

481
00:24:50,541 --> 00:24:53,416
Hi. My name's Dolly. I run Tolita.

482
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:55,625
-Tolita?
-Yes.

483
00:24:55,708 --> 00:24:57,375
Mm, hello.

484
00:24:57,458 --> 00:25:00,125
You know, that snack you introduced me to
was delicious.

485
00:25:00,208 --> 00:25:01,458
-Really?
-Mandy.

486
00:25:01,541 --> 00:25:02,750
-I wanted to say hello.
-Hi.

487
00:25:02,833 --> 00:25:04,916
The Hsueh family's youngest son,
Louis Hsueh.

488
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:06,750
-Oh, hello.
-Hello.

489
00:25:06,833 --> 00:25:09,083
Just like your brother. Good-looking guy.

490
00:25:09,166 --> 00:25:11,333
Power is his thing while I'm into money.

491
00:25:11,416 --> 00:25:13,458
Ah. How long you been a member?

492
00:25:13,541 --> 00:25:15,833
A bit over a month.
I've already made a little.

493
00:25:15,916 --> 00:25:18,291
-Ah, you're still very young.
-Yes.

494
00:25:18,375 --> 00:25:20,541
I'll leave you to chat.
There's a chairman coming.

495
00:25:20,625 --> 00:25:21,583
I need to greet him.

496
00:25:21,666 --> 00:25:23,666
In due course.
I'll share some derivatives with you.

497
00:25:23,750 --> 00:25:25,333
-Great.
-Bye.

498
00:25:25,958 --> 00:25:27,708
-Hey.
-That suit looks good on you.

499
00:25:27,791 --> 00:25:29,375
Took a while to choose it.

500
00:25:36,916 --> 00:25:39,125
Hi. Could I steal a cigarette?

501
00:25:41,458 --> 00:25:42,291
I'm all out.

502
00:25:46,125 --> 00:25:48,250
You here to steal investment clients?

503
00:25:49,666 --> 00:25:51,291
What are you talking about?

504
00:25:52,541 --> 00:25:54,375
Trading cryptocurrencies.

505
00:25:54,458 --> 00:25:55,625
Isn't that what you do?

506
00:25:56,208 --> 00:25:57,541
You're some performer.

507
00:25:58,875 --> 00:26:02,208
Every client inside
is worth hundreds of millions.

508
00:26:02,958 --> 00:26:04,458
I won't be handing them over.

509
00:26:04,541 --> 00:26:06,333
You stole one of my investors.

510
00:26:06,833 --> 00:26:08,041
That's why I came.

511
00:26:08,750 --> 00:26:10,250
I didn't steal him.

512
00:26:10,333 --> 00:26:11,916
That guy made his own decision.

513
00:26:14,333 --> 00:26:17,875
You're a new business,
yet you have so many clients.

514
00:26:17,958 --> 00:26:19,416
Are you a front for someone?

515
00:26:20,083 --> 00:26:21,500
We operate legally.

516
00:26:22,333 --> 00:26:25,625
If you wanna know the way,
I'd be happy to share it with you.

517
00:26:27,958 --> 00:26:30,541
The truth is,
our company works with Yuan Tao.

518
00:26:30,625 --> 00:26:33,708
One of its founders, William,
he's also a shareholder.

519
00:26:34,708 --> 00:26:36,500
If you'd like to join us,

520
00:26:37,291 --> 00:26:38,791
we can share the profits.

521
00:26:38,875 --> 00:26:41,041
However, there are terms.

522
00:26:42,708 --> 00:26:44,458
I thought you were legit.

523
00:26:45,458 --> 00:26:46,458
You're a scammer.

524
00:26:47,666 --> 00:26:49,291
What makes you so sure?

525
00:26:49,375 --> 00:26:51,750
You can't possibly be in with Yuan Tao.

526
00:26:52,250 --> 00:26:53,500
Do you know William?

527
00:26:58,125 --> 00:27:01,500
So it turns out you guys have
a collaboration with Yuan Tao.

528
00:27:01,583 --> 00:27:02,750
I did wonder.

529
00:27:02,833 --> 00:27:06,458
Tolita is such a young company
to have seen such growth.

530
00:27:06,958 --> 00:27:10,791
And haven't they discovered
that Tolita is heavily involved

531
00:27:10,875 --> 00:27:12,500
in financial fraud?

532
00:27:13,291 --> 00:27:14,916
Where did you hear this?

533
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:17,500
Money launderers are huge gossips.

534
00:27:17,583 --> 00:27:20,000
But don't be concerned.
I'm not going to out you.

535
00:27:20,083 --> 00:27:21,958
I just wanna make money.

536
00:27:23,333 --> 00:27:24,208
How about this?

537
00:27:24,791 --> 00:27:27,291
Now that I've shared
these clients with you,

538
00:27:28,166 --> 00:27:29,583
why don't we bring William in?

539
00:27:29,666 --> 00:27:32,333
The truth's out, so why not clean up?

540
00:27:36,625 --> 00:27:39,750
If William doesn't know
your company's running scams,

541
00:27:40,250 --> 00:27:41,833
I'll keep your secret.

542
00:27:41,916 --> 00:27:45,041
And if he does,
your secret will still be safe.

543
00:27:45,625 --> 00:27:47,916
And the profits I make
working with Yuan Tao,

544
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,125
you'll get your share.

545
00:27:49,625 --> 00:27:51,041
You got a problem with that?

546
00:27:54,833 --> 00:27:56,625
Was Hsueh's younger son there?

547
00:27:56,708 --> 00:27:57,583
Yeah.

548
00:27:57,666 --> 00:28:00,333
He claimed he made a lot of money
from investing with them.

549
00:28:00,416 --> 00:28:04,500
This Mandy knows those money launderers.
She is definitely not good.

550
00:28:04,583 --> 00:28:07,166
She wouldn't target him anyway.
He's too high up.

551
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:11,166
Must be targeting easy marks.

552
00:28:11,791 --> 00:28:13,750
And she's using me to do it.

553
00:28:14,875 --> 00:28:16,333
I can't leave her be.

554
00:28:18,500 --> 00:28:19,500
Wanna meet her?

555
00:28:19,583 --> 00:28:21,583
I don't need another enemy,

556
00:28:21,666 --> 00:28:24,625
and there are indeed many easy targets.

557
00:28:24,708 --> 00:28:27,125
But I need to confirm one thing.

558
00:28:27,208 --> 00:28:29,833
We recommend long-term investment.

559
00:28:29,916 --> 00:28:32,333
We also think that blockchain technology

560
00:28:32,416 --> 00:28:35,000
isn't just for short-term speculation.

561
00:28:35,083 --> 00:28:36,041
So, in this area,

562
00:28:36,125 --> 00:28:38,291
Yuan Tao will continue to innovate.

563
00:28:38,375 --> 00:28:40,250
BARRAGE OF NEGATIVE NEWS
TRIGGERS BLOODBATH IN CRYPTO MARKET!

564
00:28:53,958 --> 00:28:56,333
At my advanced age,

565
00:28:56,833 --> 00:29:00,916
meeting in the evening
to catch the wind is rare.

566
00:29:04,750 --> 00:29:06,750
I only drink tea now.

567
00:29:12,166 --> 00:29:13,875
Long time no see.

568
00:29:20,791 --> 00:29:22,666
To alcohol over tea.

569
00:29:27,666 --> 00:29:30,125
My father would often say

570
00:29:30,625 --> 00:29:34,041
that of all the fixers,
he admired you the most.

571
00:29:34,541 --> 00:29:38,125
You're always calculating,
yet you are also calm.

572
00:29:39,916 --> 00:29:42,500
Please, let's skip the pleasantries.

573
00:29:42,583 --> 00:29:43,916
What's there to discuss?

574
00:29:48,666 --> 00:29:51,833
I know you and Thackery are close-knit.

575
00:29:52,458 --> 00:29:54,458
You're hard to unstitch.

576
00:29:56,125 --> 00:29:58,250
I just wanna remind you

577
00:29:58,333 --> 00:30:01,166
that not taking a stand

578
00:30:01,250 --> 00:30:03,375
is also taking a stand.

579
00:30:06,916 --> 00:30:08,125
What if I…

580
00:30:08,750 --> 00:30:10,666
I chose to take a stand?

581
00:30:14,791 --> 00:30:17,833
All I know is that by not taking a stand,

582
00:30:17,916 --> 00:30:20,458
all these rumors will vanish,

583
00:30:21,166 --> 00:30:24,041
and your position will be secure.

584
00:30:24,125 --> 00:30:25,541
All I know is,

585
00:30:26,208 --> 00:30:30,458
choosing Thackery Huang
to be Fixer Celestial

586
00:30:30,541 --> 00:30:32,083
was the right choice then.

587
00:30:32,166 --> 00:30:33,583
But right now,

588
00:30:33,666 --> 00:30:37,250
insisting on letting him stay
is not a good idea.

589
00:30:39,375 --> 00:30:41,625
Don't forget Ching He's code.

590
00:30:42,500 --> 00:30:44,416
Render large issues small.

591
00:30:44,500 --> 00:30:46,083
The small ones will go.

592
00:30:50,166 --> 00:30:51,458
Hmm.

593
00:30:59,791 --> 00:31:03,958
I'm old. I can't withstand this wind.

594
00:31:04,041 --> 00:31:08,375
I won't have the good fortune
to enjoy this fine wine.

595
00:31:13,666 --> 00:31:16,625
I heard you invested in Hsin Yueh
and made a killing.

596
00:31:16,708 --> 00:31:18,125
Aren't you a shareholder?

597
00:31:19,166 --> 00:31:21,708
Mandy told me after I'd already invested.

598
00:31:22,750 --> 00:31:24,166
You keep a good secret.

599
00:31:25,333 --> 00:31:26,708
I'd like to learn from you.

600
00:31:27,291 --> 00:31:29,458
You're independent financially,

601
00:31:30,125 --> 00:31:32,208
yet retirement's not on the cards.

602
00:31:32,916 --> 00:31:35,750
It's like a round of golf.
Winning someone else's money…

603
00:31:36,250 --> 00:31:37,833
It's just like a game, isn't it?

604
00:31:39,375 --> 00:31:40,666
It's all about the win.

605
00:31:41,166 --> 00:31:42,500
Hmm? Don't you think?

606
00:31:45,583 --> 00:31:47,000
Huh, nice.

607
00:31:47,625 --> 00:31:49,041
I think I know what you're saying.

608
00:31:53,541 --> 00:31:55,791
Okay, see you at the restaurant.

609
00:31:57,833 --> 00:31:58,958
How'd it go?

610
00:31:59,041 --> 00:32:00,250
William wants to talk.

611
00:32:01,291 --> 00:32:03,000
You got there.

612
00:32:03,500 --> 00:32:06,750
So how are you going to get him
to reveal his Tolita connection?

613
00:32:06,833 --> 00:32:08,583
He now thinks I'm a scammer.

614
00:32:09,208 --> 00:32:12,125
If he wants to collaborate,
Tolita has to come in.

615
00:32:12,208 --> 00:32:13,250
Oh.

616
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:15,833
If he won't collaborate,

617
00:32:15,916 --> 00:32:18,791
he'll ask you
not to reveal Tolita's scam activity,

618
00:32:18,875 --> 00:32:21,666
which is proof that he is connected
to this company, right?

619
00:32:26,791 --> 00:32:29,541
It's such a shame
that you work as a fixer.

620
00:32:29,625 --> 00:32:31,458
If I'd met you sooner, damn.

621
00:32:31,541 --> 00:32:33,625
The gambling joint would have thrived.

622
00:32:34,833 --> 00:32:36,083
Genius.

623
00:32:37,125 --> 00:32:38,333
Ah.

624
00:32:51,833 --> 00:32:54,375
Felix said
you're meeting with William tomorrow.

625
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:55,833
Mm.

626
00:32:56,708 --> 00:32:57,791
Tomorrow night.

627
00:33:01,208 --> 00:33:02,666
What's on your mind?

628
00:33:03,833 --> 00:33:06,250
This whole investigation till now.

629
00:33:07,250 --> 00:33:08,375
What do I do

630
00:33:08,458 --> 00:33:12,083
if the outcome's not what I want it to be?

631
00:33:17,125 --> 00:33:18,250
Ben made this for you.

632
00:33:18,333 --> 00:33:20,541
No radishes, no pork meatballs.

633
00:33:24,416 --> 00:33:27,125
You know, if I don't order it from him,

634
00:33:27,625 --> 00:33:29,291
he won't offer it to me.

635
00:33:30,375 --> 00:33:31,583
Enjoy it.

636
00:33:36,750 --> 00:33:38,166
What's in this for you?

637
00:33:38,250 --> 00:33:39,833
Being a fixer?

638
00:33:44,333 --> 00:33:47,166
If my brother ever has a problem
he can't handle,

639
00:33:47,250 --> 00:33:48,958
I can help him take care of it.

640
00:33:49,583 --> 00:33:52,291
Then my dad will know he has two sons.

641
00:33:58,625 --> 00:34:00,333
Tomorrow will go smoothly.

642
00:34:20,500 --> 00:34:22,458
You've gotten better.

643
00:34:23,250 --> 00:34:26,125
Ten to seven. You're off your game today.

644
00:34:26,208 --> 00:34:28,125
I thought I'd let you win today.

645
00:34:28,208 --> 00:34:31,208
If you shut down because of me,
I'll have nowhere to play.

646
00:34:31,291 --> 00:34:33,041
-This is for you.
-Oh, thank you.

647
00:34:33,125 --> 00:34:34,750
-Ah.
-Gun for you.

648
00:34:34,833 --> 00:34:37,208
-Go home and practice.
-First time I got this.

649
00:34:37,291 --> 00:34:39,000
-Come on, let's eat.
-All right.

650
00:34:39,666 --> 00:34:42,875
I know I haven't been here for a while,
but these prices are ridiculous.

651
00:34:46,333 --> 00:34:48,541
Okay. The food all right?

652
00:34:48,625 --> 00:34:50,750
Why did I win?

653
00:34:52,208 --> 00:34:54,041
I should lose to you.

654
00:34:54,125 --> 00:34:56,250
I'm growing old. You're growing up.

655
00:34:58,125 --> 00:34:59,625
Why won't you tell Mom you're sick?

656
00:35:00,750 --> 00:35:03,375
Telling her now
will only make her more worried.

657
00:35:03,958 --> 00:35:05,666
I looked it up online.

658
00:35:05,750 --> 00:35:08,041
Parkinson's just gets worse, you know?

659
00:35:10,125 --> 00:35:11,583
Of course I know.

660
00:35:13,250 --> 00:35:18,375
And so, there'll be a day
when your mom will be your responsibility.

661
00:35:18,458 --> 00:35:19,291
Stop that.

662
00:35:20,166 --> 00:35:21,500
Don't underrate me, okay?

663
00:35:21,583 --> 00:35:25,416
I can take care of you, too,
and Mom's stronger than you think as well.

664
00:35:26,458 --> 00:35:27,875
I don't need you to tell me.

665
00:35:27,958 --> 00:35:30,541
When she's mad, I know to stay well away.

666
00:35:32,166 --> 00:35:34,916
You should decide
what to give Mom for her birthday.

667
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:36,750
I know, and I got her a gift.

668
00:35:36,833 --> 00:35:37,708
Oh.

669
00:35:37,791 --> 00:35:39,458
She'll love it.

670
00:35:40,833 --> 00:35:42,541
Mm. Eat quickly.

671
00:35:42,625 --> 00:35:44,916
We've gotta get the sticky tofu
for your mom.

672
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Then hurry up and get it.
Your chicken cutlet will take a while.

673
00:35:48,083 --> 00:35:49,541
Yeah, good idea.

674
00:35:49,625 --> 00:35:53,375
You can eat the noodles,
but the chicken cutlet is off-limits.

675
00:35:53,458 --> 00:35:54,583
You hear me?

676
00:35:59,791 --> 00:36:03,000
The plane ticket is booked.
Counting down to going abroad.

677
00:36:03,083 --> 00:36:04,583
Don't miss me too much.

678
00:36:18,458 --> 00:36:20,250
Yes, yes, okay.

679
00:36:20,333 --> 00:36:21,458
Uh-huh.

680
00:36:21,541 --> 00:36:22,916
Yeah. Okay, bye.

681
00:36:35,500 --> 00:36:37,166
Fuck! What is that?

682
00:36:54,666 --> 00:36:58,250
We'll follow party protocol.
There'll be no special consideration.

683
00:36:58,333 --> 00:37:01,041
We cannot waver
due to changes in the political wind,

684
00:37:01,125 --> 00:37:05,166
nor can we let an isolated incident
cloud our determination for reform.

685
00:37:10,041 --> 00:37:12,375
As for my father, he is in good health.

686
00:37:12,458 --> 00:37:15,041
He continues to care about society
and about people.

687
00:37:15,125 --> 00:37:16,500
I'd like to thank everyone.

688
00:37:16,583 --> 00:37:18,583
We now have breaking news.

689
00:37:33,750 --> 00:37:36,041
Don't wait. He won't be there.

690
00:37:37,750 --> 00:37:40,458
Search and rescue personnel
found the body in the mountains.

691
00:37:40,541 --> 00:37:44,250
The exact cause and motive of death
are yet to be determined.

692
00:37:44,333 --> 00:37:47,833
The sudden news of this tragedy
has shocked the business world.

693
00:37:47,916 --> 00:37:51,458
Yuan Tao will be releasing a statement
later this evening.

694
00:38:24,458 --> 00:38:25,291
Fuck!
